BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Bandwagon Summer Series: Bywater Call
DTSTART:20260814T180000
DTEND:20260814T200000
DTSTAMP:20260814T120301Z
UID:4642d819f068f882f9bc83634888c3@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Bywater Call is a seven-piece Southern soul and roots rock ban
 d from Toronto known for electrifying live performances\, soaring vocals\,
  and rich musical chemistry. Fronted by powerhouse vocalist Meghan Parnell
 \, the band blends soul\, R&amp\;B\, roots rock\, and Americana into a dyn
 amic sound that ranges from intimate ballads to high-energy anthems. Fresh
  off extensive international touring and recognized with UK Blues Award no
 minations for International Blues Artist of the Year\, Bywater Call delive
 rs an unforgettable concert experience filled with passion\, power\, and e
 xceptional musicianship.\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Location: Southern Vermont
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/bandwagon-
 summer-series-bywater-call-10-07-2026-21-04-56
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Central Vermont Chamber Music Festival presents Erik Friedlander: 
 Block Ice & Propane
DTSTART:20260814T190000
DTEND:20260814T210000
DTSTAMP:20260814T120301Z
UID:d5f929d631e30e87161a708e86791f@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:On Friday\, August 14\, experience a special evening of the Ce
 ntral Vermont Chamber Music Festival with cellist Erik Friedlander!<br/><b
 r/>Block Ice &amp\; Propane is a vivid musical road journal\, a collection
  of pieces that evoke endless interstate drives\, small-town truck stops\,
  and the wide\, open stretches of the American landscape. Drawing from Ame
 rican roots and folk traditions\, Friedlander shapes these influences into
  a sound that is distinctly his own.<br/><br/>The project is grounded in m
 emories of childhood cross-country trips with his family\, and that sense 
 of movement\, distance\, and discovery runs throughout the music. These pe
 rsonal reflections are paired with visual elements\, including photographs
  by his father\, renowned photographer Lee Friedlander\, and films by Bill
  Morrison\, whose work explores time\, memory\, and decay. Together\, they
  form a layered portrait of American travel that feels part documentary\, 
 part dream.<br/><br/>On the cello\, Friedlander employs an intricate finge
 rpicking technique and resonant open tunings more often associated with gu
 itar and folk styles. This approach gives the instrument a rugged\, earthy
  quality while maintaining a spacious\, lyrical feel. The result is a kind
  of new American cello music that feels both familiar and unexpected\, dir
 ect in its melodic language yet emotionally rich\, reflective\, and quietl
 y haunting.\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Location: Central Vermont
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/central-ve
 rmont-chamber-music-festival-presents-erik-friedlander-block-ice-amp-propa
 ne-02-05-2026-14-35-21
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Chickweed
DTSTART:20260814T180000
DTEND:20260814T200000
DTSTAMP:20260814T120301Z
UID:664fdd891cc4b331285848e5c75c07@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Live Concert on the Academy Green\, August 14th\, at 6pm<br/>A
 dmission by Donation <br/>Featuring CALEX Food Truck<br/><br/>Chickweed is
  a women’s trio that brings the perfect blend of rhythm\, vocal harmonie
 s\, and song writing to their roots in Latin\, Jazz\, Folk\, and Blues. Li
 nda Warnaar\, Fran Forim\, and Abby Maier Johnson have been playing togeth
 er for nearly 15 years. They will be playing some covers you can sing alon
 g with and originals from their new album “Back Home Again\,” recorded
  by McIndoes Academy member John Heartson. <br/>Quoting John Heartson\, "W
 hat a great group of musicians. Linda Warnaar is an incredible songwriter 
 and an extremely versatile musician. I can't get these songs out of my hea
 d."\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Food & Drink
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/chickweed-
 09-07-2026-14-21-26
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Summer Concert Series: The Eyetraps
DTSTART:20260814T123000
DTEND:20260814T133000
DTSTAMP:20260814T120301Z
UID:5841c2876884dc49f97364436988ed@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Alex Frantz and Zack Shafer spent five years writing and perfo
 rming together before relocating from Ohio to Vermont and forming The Eyet
 raps with bassist Phil Smith and drummer Sophie Powell. Drawing inspiratio
 n from ’90s grunge and modern indie rock\, the band’s self-titled debu
 t EP features heavy distorted guitars\, raw vocals\, and stacked harmonies
  exploring themes of regret\, loss\, and self-deception. <br/><br/>A seaso
 nal celebration of Vermont’s incredible musicians\, the Summer Concert S
 eries has been serving up a side of local music to downtown Burlington at 
 lunchtime for 14 years. <br/><br/>Summer in the City is made possible in p
 art thanks to Underwriters at the Pomerleau Family Foundation\; Supporters
  Burlington Telecom\, Myti\, Soundtoys\, and Lake Champlain Chocolates\, a
 nd Community Partner American Flatbread Burlington &amp\; Mothership Brewe
 ry. Media Sponsors: Seven Days and WCAX.⁠\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Music: Rock\, Folk\, Jazz and More
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/summer-con
 cert-series-the-eyetraps-19-06-2026-20-18-44
END:VEVENT
