BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:You're a Good Man\, Charlie Brown
DTSTART:20260814T110000
DTEND:20260814T123000
DTSTAMP:20260814T120301Z
UID:3ad6699fcf7f04bca8bb6df5d7be2c@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Based on the beloved Peanuts comic strip by Charles M. Schulz\
 , this charming musical brings Charlie Brown\, Snoopy\, Lucy\, Linus\, and
  the rest of the gang to life in a heartwarming celebration of friendship\
 , imagination\, and the joys of everyday life.<br/><br/>This production wi
 ll be performed outdoors in a partially shaded area. Chair seating will be
  available\; however\, a reservation does not guarantee a chair. Audience 
 members are encouraged to bring a blanket or lawn chair for their comfort.
 \n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Theater & Dance
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/youre-a-go
 od-man-charlie-brown-21-07-2026-15-03-50
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:2026 Area Choir Summer Sing
DTSTART:20260815T093000
DTEND:20260815T113000
DTSTAMP:20260814T120301Z
UID:cd42c039c02421e527beebc27f4d55@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:2026 Area Choir Summer Sing<br/><br/>The Area Choir announces 
 a return of their Summer Sing on Saturday\, August 15th from 9:30-11:30 AM
  at South Congregational Church\, 20 Church St.\, Newport NH. Come share a
  morning of singing with those who enjoy making music together.<br/><br/>T
 here is no fee\, no audition\, no performance and the Summer Sing is open 
 to everyone. Susan Cancio-Bello\, Area Choir Director of Music\, has plann
 ed a spirited assortment of music for all abilities\, with Alex Stewart ac
 companying on the piano.<br/><br/>To help us plan for enough copies of mus
 ic\, we encourage registration by emailing TheAreaChoir@gmail.com with you
 r name and contact information. Walk-ins are also fine on the morning of A
 ugust 15 th . For more information contact Karen Little at 603-863-4007 or
  Susan Cancio-Bello at 603-848-8898.\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Classes & Workshops
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/2026-area-
 choir-summer-sing-13-07-2026-17-06-24
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Castleton Colonial Day Historic House Tour
DTSTART:20260815T100000
DTEND:20260815T150000
DTSTAMP:20260814T120301Z
UID:535422bc4161aff9e5db146a080b79@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Castleton Colonial Day Historic House Tour<br/>Step back in ti
 me as hostesses in Colonial attire greet guests in homes along Castleton h
 istoric Main Street during the 86th Annual Colonial Day Historic House Tou
 r\, Saturday August 15\, 2026. This annual event featuring over a dozen si
 tes throughout the village including outstanding period homes\, public bui
 ldings and historic sites.<br/>The Federated Church on Main Street\, descr
 ibed as builder Thomas Royal Dake’s architectural masterpiece\, is a pop
 ular stop on the tour. The pulpit\, with its intricate moldings and panels
  is one of the most extraordinary in the state. Dake is famous for his bea
 utifully scaled spiral staircases which can be seen in some of the homes o
 n the tour. <br/>There will be a quilt display at the Church as well.<br/>
 At the Higley House\, home of the Castleton Historical Society\, visitors 
 can tour the exhibits\, antique tools\, carriage collection and period fas
 hion display of 19th century clothing and accessories. On display at the H
 igley House will be the famous Blue Cat Quilt depicting historic landmarks
  in town and highlights from the book The Blue Cat of Castleton. The 2026 
 Castleton Colonial Day Historic House Tour will be held rain or shine Satu
 rday\, August 15th from 10am to 3pm. Tour tickets $25 can be purchased on 
 Colonial Day at ticket booths on Main Street. For information visit websit
 e at www.castletonhistorichousetour.org or call 802-468-5691. <br/>\n\nSou
 rces: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Location: Addison/Rutland
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/castleton-
 colonial-day-historic-house-tour-26-04-2026-13-47-55
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Jamaica Day 2026
DTSTART:20260815T090000
DTEND:20260815T180000
DTSTAMP:20260814T120301Z
UID:ec9079ffd3355812f145c84a9758c6@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Hosted by the Jamaica Historical Foundation\, Jamaica Day carr
 ies on the cherished tradition of Old Home Days\, bringing neighbors\, for
 mer residents\, and visitors together for a day of small-town celebration.
 <br/><br/>Spend the day enjoying:<br/><br/>☼ A festive community parade<
 br/>☼ Live music throughout the day<br/>☼ Local food and craft vendors
 <br/>☼ A quilt show and raffle<br/>☼ Children's activities and games<b
 r/>☼ Historical exhibits and demonstrations<br/>☼ Free cake and a town
 -wide community photo<br/>☼ And much more!<br/><br/>Whether you're a lon
 gtime local or visiting for the weekend\, Jamaica Day is a chance to celeb
 rate the people\, history\, and traditions that make Jamaica\, Vermont suc
 h a special place.<br/><br/>Join us as we celebrate Jamaica's past\, prese
 nt\, and future!\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Fairs\, Festivals & Markets
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/jamaica-da
 y-2026-13-07-2026-14-36-02
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Shelburne Day at Farmers Market
DTSTART:20260815T090000
DTEND:20260815T140000
DTSTAMP:20260814T120301Z
UID:b3817ebd62c6c67fea17480d6d2499@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Shelburne Day is an oversize Farmers Market\, on the parade gr
 ounds\, the village green and in front of many of our shops. Come down for
  locally grown veggies\, handmade crafts\, an outdoor yoga class\, music\,
  outdoor sales and more. Come join in the fun!\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Fairs\, Festivals & Markets
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/shelburne-
 day-at-farmers-market-30-07-2026-10-59-37
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Single Signature Bookbinding
DTSTART:20260815T100000
DTEND:20260815T130000
DTSTAMP:20260814T120301Z
UID:19634a32d17c9a748f8ea412f90149@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:In this beginner-level workshop\, you'll learn how to construc
 t a single-signature book with a hard cover. You'll learn basic book bindi
 ng techniques that will enable you to start creating unique books to use f
 or journaling\, sketches\, poems\, photos\, and more. We'll add a couple o
 f pockets on the inside\, and you can finish the book off with beads or a 
 design of your choice on the front. You'll have a variety of papers to cho
 ose from for your cover\, or you can bring some of your favorite papers.\n
 \nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Classes & Workshops
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/single-sig
 nature-bookbinding-01-07-2026-14-06-48
END:VEVENT
